        ENGLISH.put("Instant Caption ",R.string.ui_instant_caption_b7cd0b00);
        ENGLISH.put("\nSpeech recognition and AI translation run locally on your phone and work offline once models are ready.\nSpeech models recognize audio; Qwen NPU or OPUS-MT CPU translates text. Some OPUS-MT routes require a Whisper English bridge.\nModel downloads require a network connection; captions are not sent to an external translation service.",R.string.ui_speech_recognition_and_ai_translation_run_lo_ad43b34b);
        ENGLISH.put("Transcript exported",R.string.ui_transcript_exported_fb9fa2d0);
        ENGLISH.put("Use Microphone for live speech, or Device audio for video and streaming apps. Some apps block audio capture. Floating captions work over other apps. Drag anywhere, tuck at either edge and tap the handle to expand.\n\nChoose speech, caption and interface languages and font sizes independently. Speech recognition and text translation have separate model pages with download, selection and removal. Choices are saved.\n\nQwen3-0.6B / 1.7B / 4B: selectable multilingual NPU text translation directly from recognized source text, without an English bridge. This bundle requires SM8750 / SM8850, Android 15+ and at least 8 GB RAM. The 4B model requires at least 12 GB RAM. See each model for its size. Loading takes a few seconds before recording.\n\nOPUS-MT: smaller CPU language packs for Chinese, German, French, Spanish, Russian, Arabic, Hindi, Italian and Portuguese. Non-English speech first uses Whisper to produce English; English captions use its output directly. Small bridge models may mistranslate.\n\nAutomatic recognition reuses installed system offline packs, otherwise a compatible local model. You can also select a speech model manually. If a changed translation route is incompatible with your manual speech choice, select a compatible model or Automatic.\n\nCompatible NPU models are labeled and recommended first. Portable CPU models serve other compatible phones. Downloading a spare model does not change the selection. All speech and captions are processed locally; only downloads need networking. Backup channels, resume and SHA-256 verification are supported.\n\nSpeech only: environmental sound labels are filtered, but background speech or singing can still be recognized. Drafts are revised; quality and latency vary by language, phone and recording conditions.",R.string.ui_use_microphone_for_live_speech_or_device_aud_f9964f9b);
